---
import Layout from "@components/Layout.astro";
import PageHeader from "@components/PageHeader.astro";
import DecklistTooltip from "@components/DecklistTooltip.astro";
import { Card, Badge, Alert } from "webcoreui/astro";
---

<Layout
    title="Intuition Guide - Replenish Guide"
    description="Master the art of Intuition in Replenish. Discover common pile patterns, engine setups, and complex situational plays to maximize your card selection."
>
    <PageHeader
        title="The Intuition Guide"
        description="<strong>A few tips:</strong> Intuition is a skill-intensive card, and it might take some time to learn all the possible lines that the card enables, as it plays multiple critical roles throughout a game. A fundamental rule of Intuition is the tradeoff between immediacy and future availability: when you tutor for a non-combo piece (like removal or a sideboard card), you are effectively removing three copies of that card from your deck to guarantee access to one. Keep in mind also when you are building your deck that any card you intend to reliably fetch with Intuition requires you to run at least 3 copies in your 75."
        imageSrc="/src/assets/banners/intuition.jpeg"
        imageAlt="Intuition"
        imageCaption="Intuition by April Lee"
        isCard={true}
    />
    <Card title="Core Mechanics: Hand vs. Graveyard Enforcement" titleTag="h2">
        <p>
            Because your opponent decides which card enters your hand and which
            are discarded to your graveyard, you must construct piles with
            precise redundancy depending on your intended destination:
        </p>

        <div
            style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.5rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"
        >
            <div>
                <h3
                    style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0; color: var(--w-color-primary-10); font-size: 1.2rem;"
                >
                    Enforce to Hand
                </h3>
                <p style="margin: 0;">
                    When you need a specific answer or threat in your hand
                    immediately upon resolution (such as spot removal or a
                    sideboard answer), your pile must contain <strong
                        >3 identical copies</strong
                    > or 3 functionally redundant cards. Consequently, any silver
                    bullet you intend to reliably tutor with <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Intuition">Intuition</a
                    > requires running at least 3 copies in your 75.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div>
                <h3
                    style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0; color: var(--w-color-primary-10); font-size: 1.2rem;"
                >
                    Enforce to Graveyard
                </h3>
                <p style="margin: 0;">
                    When your tactical goal is depositing a specific combo
                    enchantment directly into the graveyard for an upcoming <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Replenish">Replenish</a
                    >, your pile only needs <strong>2 copies</strong> of that target.
                    Regardless of which card the opponent gives to your hand, at least
                    one copy is mathematically guaranteed to reach the yard.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            <Alert theme="warning">
                <strong>Incomplete Piles & Deck Tracking</strong><br />
                If you have already drawn a copy of a card you desperately need in
                hand (leaving only two in your library), pair those two copies with
                a high-priority threat like <a
                    href="#"
                    class="card-hover"
                    data-card-name="Parallax Wave">Parallax Wave</a
                > to force a lose-lose choice for your opponent. Always mentally track
                your remaining deck contents before resolving Intuition so you never
                end up with a broken pile.
            </Alert>
        </div>
    </Card>

    <Card title="General Heuristics & Timing" titleTag="h2">
        <p>
            <strong>Post-Sideboard Role Shift & On-Stack Hate:</strong> When confronting
            permanent graveyard hate like <a
                href="#"
                class="card-hover"
                data-card-name="Tormod's Crypt">Tormod's Crypt</a
            >, <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Phyrexian Furnace"
                >Phyrexian Furnace</a
            >, or <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Planar Void"
                >Planar Void</a
            >, never construct combo-dumping piles blind. Intuition shifts out
            of its graveyard selection role and transforms into a targeted spot
            removal tutor—searching for three copies of <a
                href="#"
                class="card-hover"
                data-card-name="Seal of Cleansing">Seal of Cleansing</a
            > or <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Disenchant"
                >Disenchant</a
            > to systematically dismantle opposing graveyard interruption before you
            resume combo assembly.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">
            <strong>Deck Depletion & Managing Threat Density:</strong> In prolonged
            attrition games against traditional Control structures, be wary of aggressive
            over-tutoring. Because Intuition purges cards from your library in sets
            of three—amplified by heavy looting from <a
                href="#"
                class="card-hover"
                data-card-name="Attunement">Attunement</a
            > and <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Frantic Search"
                >Frantic Search</a
            >—you risk depleting your overall win-condition density or falling
            prey to deck-out fatigue if your initial reanimation lines are
            countered. Recognize when to pivot from deck thinning to preserving
            your remaining resource volume.
        </p>
    </Card>

    <Card title="Common Tactical Piles" titleTag="h2">
        <p style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
            Below are standard tactical configurations and when to deploy them
            during tournament matches:
        </p>

        <div
            style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;"
        >
            <div
                style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(150, 150, 150, 0.2); padding-bottom: 1.5rem;"
            >
                <div
                    style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap;"
                >
                    <h3 style="margin: 0; color: var(--w-color-primary-10);">
                        Dumping Combo Pieces
                    </h3>
                    <Badge theme="secondary" small={true}
                        >Enforce to Graveyard</Badge
                    >
                </div>
                <p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
                    The primary engine setup when holding <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Replenish">Replenish</a
                    > paired with a discard outlet (<a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Attunement">Attunement</a
                    > or <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Frantic Search">Frantic Search</a
                    >). If an enchantment absolutely must reach the graveyard
                    immediately to fuel your upcoming untap, include at least
                    two copies in your trio.
                </p>
                <div
                    style="background-color: var(--w-color-primary-95); padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: var(--w-md-radius); font-size: 0.95rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--w-color-primary-40);"
                >
                    <strong>Standard Configurations:</strong>
                    <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Opalescence"
                        >Opal</a
                    > + <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Decree of Silence">Decree</a
                    > + <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Parallax Wave">Wave</a
                    >
                    (balanced lock), <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Opalescence">Opal</a
                    > + <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Opalescence">Opal</a
                    > + <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Parallax Wave">Wave</a
                    > (guaranteed Opal in yard/hand), or <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Parallax Wave">Wave</a
                    > x3 (when fighting explosive aggression).
                </div>
            </div>

            <div
                style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(150, 150, 150, 0.2); padding-bottom: 1.5rem;"
            >
                <div
                    style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap;"
                >
                    <h3 style="margin: 0; color: var(--w-color-primary-10);">
                        Split Piles: The Lose-Lose Dilemma
                    </h3>
                    <Badge theme="secondary" small={true}>Enforce to Hand</Badge
                    >
                </div>
                <p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
                    In mid-to-late game board states, you can abandon strict
                    redundancy and instead construct a pile of three completely
                    different, highly synergistic threats. By tutoring for a
                    combination where discarded enchantments feed an
                    accompanying reanimation spell or card selection engine, you
                    force your opponent into an uncomfortable lose-lose choice
                    where every outcome advances your win condition.
                </p>
                <div
                    style="background-color: var(--w-color-primary-95); padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: var(--w-md-radius); font-size: 0.95rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--w-color-primary-40);"
                >
                    <strong>Standard Configurations:</strong>
                    <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Replenish"
                        >Replenish</a
                    > + <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Attunement">Attunement</a
                    > + <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Parallax Wave">Wave</a
                    > (if they give you Replenish, you immediately animate Attunement
                    and Wave; if they give you Attunement or Wave, you secure powerful
                    on-board engines).
                </div>
            </div>

            <div
                style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(150, 150, 150, 0.2); padding-bottom: 1.5rem;"
            >
                <div
                    style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap;"
                >
                    <h3 style="margin: 0; color: var(--w-color-primary-10);">
                        Tutoring Targeted Removal
                    </h3>
                    <Badge theme="secondary" small={true}>Enforce to Hand</Badge
                    >
                </div>
                <p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
                    Because <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Swords to Plowshares"
                        >Swords to Plowshares</a
                    > and <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Seal of Cleansing">Seal of Cleansing</a
                    > answer fundamentally different threat axes, your selection must
                    precisely target the battlefield problem. Tutor for three Swords
                    when facing lethal aggressive creature clocks. Tutor for three
                    Seals when breaking through oppressive lock pieces; as a major
                    synergy bonus, discarded Seals will reanimate to the battlefield
                    for free upon resolving your next <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Replenish">Replenish</a
                    >.
                </p>
                <div
                    style="background-color: var(--w-color-primary-95); padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: var(--w-md-radius); font-size: 0.95rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--w-color-primary-40);"
                >
                    <strong>Standard Configurations:</strong>
                    <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Swords to Plowshares"
                        >Swords to Plowshares</a
                    > x3 (anti-creature), <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Seal of Cleansing">Seal of Cleansing</a
                    > x3 (anti-artifact/enchantment).
                </div>
            </div>

            <div
                style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(150, 150, 150, 0.2); padding-bottom: 1.5rem;"
            >
                <div
                    style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap;"
                >
                    <h3 style="margin: 0; color: var(--w-color-primary-10);">
                        Guaranteeing Land Drops & Deck Thinning
                    </h3>
                    <Badge theme="secondary" small={true}>Enforce to Hand</Badge
                    >
                </div>
                <p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
                    In early developmental turns, enforcing a land drop prevents
                    fatal tempo stumbles when holding an otherwise lethal hand.
                    Furthermore, during prolonged attrition battles against slow
                    Control opponents, tutoring for three lands serves as
                    strategic deck-thinning—pulling dead lands out of your
                    library so your subsequent draws yield a significantly
                    higher density of live threats and countermagic.
                </p>
                <div
                    style="background-color: var(--w-color-primary-95); padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: var(--w-md-radius); font-size: 0.95rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--w-color-primary-40);"
                >
                    <strong>Standard Configurations:</strong>
                    <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Ancient Tomb"
                        >Ancient Tomb</a
                    > x3, <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Skycloud Expanse">Skycloud Expanse</a
                    > x3, <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Plains"
                        >Plains</a
                    > x3.
                </div>
            </div>

            <div
                style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(150, 150, 150, 0.2); padding-bottom: 1.5rem;"
            >
                <div
                    style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap;"
                >
                    <h3 style="margin: 0; color: var(--w-color-primary-10);">
                        Finding a Discard Engine
                    </h3>
                    <Badge theme="secondary" small={true}>Enforce to Hand</Badge
                    >
                </div>
                <p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
                    When your hand is saturated with heavy combo enchantments
                    and <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Replenish">Replenish</a
                    > but lacks a reliable outlet to discard them, utilize Intuition
                    to immediately secure a card selection engine and unlock your
                    operational lines.
                </p>
                <div
                    style="background-color: var(--w-color-primary-95); padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: var(--w-md-radius); font-size: 0.95rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--w-color-primary-40);"
                >
                    <strong>Standard Configurations:</strong>
                    <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Frantic Search">Frantic Search</a
                    > x3, <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Attunement">Attunement</a
                    > x3.
                </div>
            </div>

            <div>
                <div
                    style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap;"
                >
                    <h3 style="margin: 0; color: var(--w-color-primary-10);">
                        Tutoring Sideboard Tech
                    </h3>
                    <Badge theme="secondary" small={true}>Enforce to Hand</Badge
                    >
                </div>
                <p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
                    In high-stakes games 2 and 3, grabbing three exact copies of
                    a meta-breaking sideboard piece allows you to sever opposing
                    countermagic suites, disable taxing utility lands, or
                    paralyze enemy combo setups on demand.
                </p>
                <div
                    style="background-color: var(--w-color-primary-95); padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: var(--w-md-radius); font-size: 0.95rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--w-color-primary-40);"
                >
                    <strong>Standard Configurations:</strong>
                    <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Meddling Mage">Meddling Mage</a
                    > x3, <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Abeyance">Abeyance</a
                    > x3, <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Tsabo's Web">Tsabo's Web</a
                    > x3.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </Card>
    <DecklistTooltip />
</Layout>
